-- Date Functions in SQL
-- Date Functions are built-in SQL functions used to extract, format, calculate, compare, and manipulate dates and times.

| Function       | Purpose                               |
| ---------------| ------------------------------------- |
| CURDATE()      | Returns the current date              |
| NOW()          | Returns current date and time         |
| YEAR()         | Extracts the year                     |
| MONTH()        | Extracts the month                    |
| MONTHNAME()    | Returns the month name                |
| DAY()          | Extracts the day                      |
| DAYNAME()      | Returns the day name                  |
| DAYOFWEEK()    | Returns weekday number                |
| DAYOFYEAR()    | Returns day number of the year        |
| DATEDIFF()     | Finds difference between two dates    |
| QUARTER()      | Returns the quarter                   |

